\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Reference measure for real fields}
\date{2026-10-30}

\p{On the [alternating four-cycle](fdip-0003), a real field has four
coordinates #{\phi(v)}, one for each #{v\in V=\{0,1,2,3\}}.
The [coordinate reference measure](fdip-002H) assigns the unit field box
#{[0,1]^V=\{\phi:0\leq\phi(v)\leq1\text{ for every }v\in V\}}
the volume
##{\lambda_V([0,1]^V)=1.}
This is the product of four interval lengths. The edge weights and mass
do not enter this volume; the whole field space has infinite measure.}

\p{The [real field topology](fdip-002C) and its [Borel sets](fdip-002D)
make coordinate maps measurable. [Reindexing and splitting](fdip-002J)
preserve product volume, while [linear changes](fdip-002K) require a
Jacobian. A [subspace's induced volume](fdip-002M) supplies its own
reference measure. These conventions determine the integrals defining
[positive Gaussian laws](fdip-0017) and [constrained massless laws](fdip-003V).}

